Credential Stuffing Solution (picoCTF 2026)
Credential Stuffing by David Gaviria is a Web Exploitation challenge that simulates a real-world attack where leaked credentials from one breach are tested against another service to find reused passwords. 

Challenge Mechanics
Unlike the "Hashgate" challenge which relied on IDOR, this challenge requires you to automate login attempts against a netcat service using a provided list of stolen credentials (creds-dump.txt). 

Target: nc crystal-peak.picoctf.net 63106
Input: A text file containing thousands of username;password pairs. 
Goal: Find the single pair that successfully logs into the bank portal and retrieves the flag.
Constraint: The service may disconnect or rate-limit rapid connections, requiring a scripted approach rather than manual testing. 

